{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact head fb9fdbd1462da4721c556b6d72d84c2a6324d68f, tree d3a8e293064ef5b9bac73e68c50e7048cc87b00a, on builder/xd1-classes-20261116, all 5 artifacts, for request 29ba4226 under my promise 544b9836. This verdict names the one implementation: XD-1 steps 2 and 3 (request 248e0c6e, promise 2694899f, report bec1551c, the XD-1 note, primary). `gs review --prepare` resolved that binding at this head, with the request closing on the sealed receipt. Main 5394563c is the base, and one commit changes five paths.\n\nWhat I read:\n\n- The guard. `classOf` gives `no-owner` when no test context holds the controller, `stale` when the owner finished, and `lost` when the owner still runs. The guard prints one line with the class first. A `lost` refusal returns, so `rejectTimeoutError` goes on and Vitest fails the test with its own timeout error. A `stale` or `no-owner` refusal is thrown again, as before. A refusal with any other reason is thrown again unchanged.\n- The setup file. `beforeEach` registers the owner with `finished: false`, and `afterEach` sets `finished`. The setup file's hooks are registered before a test file's own hooks. So a timeout in a test file's own `beforeEach` or `afterEach` aborts an owner that is still running, and it counts as `lost`, which is right.\n- `scripts/gate.sh`. It prints one count for each class and fails the gate only when `lost` is above zero. It keeps an earlier failure.\n- The control. Seven Node cases pin each class, the owner of a late timer, the unwrapped refusal, the quiet cases, and the fixed prefix that the gate counts.\n- The note. The first paragraph now says that the lost rejection is possible by source and that every line so far is a stale timer. \"Read the line\" says that a `beforeAll` or `afterAll` timer reports `no-owner`. Both points of my review 7bc4ba09 are in. The new Limit section says that a timer that fires between the settle and `afterEach` counts as `lost` and fails the gate, although the test passed.\n\nWhat I checked:\n\n- Scope. The 5 artifacts name the head, no path repeats, and their paths equal `git diff --no-renames --name-only 5394563c fb9fdbd1`.\n- The gate, END b9dd464b, on this exact head. `/Users/hughpyle/play/artroom-evidence/2026-11-16-xd1-classes-gate/gate.log` names head fb9fdbd1 and tree d3a8e293 with 0 changed files. Pins passed in 17.3 s. Plain 4957 with 1 skipped and Native 1173 with 2 skipped passed. The crossing counts were lost 0, stale 3 and no-owner 0, and the last line is \"gate passed\". The three lines name owners in the `xd1-owner-20261116` worktree directory, which the gate reused at this head.\n- Cheap checks. The commit-message check passes: 1 checked, 0 flagged. `check-notes` gives 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. I ran no tests.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The class comes from the owner's own state, which the setup file sets in Vitest's own hooks. The gate fails only on a timeout that Vitest would otherwise lose.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The change touches only test support, the gate script and a Node test.\n\nSimplification: no required change.\n\nOne risk for the planner, not blocking: the Limit case is a real false failure. A `lost` line in a gate whose test passed is either that case or a real lost timeout, and the line alone cannot tell them apart. The note says so. If a gate fails on a `lost` line, read the recorded duration against the limit before you treat it as a slow test.\n\nThis approval authorizes no push, landing or deployment. The planner decides the landing.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bec1551c9fe8ca73e42996c70af665c95f487bf2","binding":"assigned","head":"fb9fdbd1462da4721c556b6d72d84c2a6324d68f","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:544b9836347ceb761605b5ad54c2dfe88f33efaf\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:2694899fff8389884b44127b53fa801